        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> > Input picker name is slow. It would be better to open a picker for selecting from registry and retain the previous query.\r\n> \r\n> This can also be achieved because registry is available to the user. I'd suggest either using `MiniPick.ui_select()` to get the registry entry name or supply `completion` to ` vim.fn.input()`.\r\n\r\nThanks for the suggestion. \r\n```lua\r\n  local switch_picker = function()\r\n    local query = MiniPick.get_picker_query() or {}\r\n    MiniPick.stop()\r\n    MiniPick.ui_select(vim.tbl_keys(MiniPick.registry), {\r\n      prompt = 'Switch picker with query: ' .. table.concat(query, ''),\r\n    }, function(picker)\r\n      vim.cmd('Pick ' .. picker)\r\n      local transfer_query = function() MiniPick.set_picker_query(query) end\r\n      vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', { pattern = 'MiniPickStart', once = true, callback = transfer_query })\r\n    end)\r\n  end\r\n  require('mini.pick').setup({\r\n    mappings = {\r\n      switch = { char = '<C-k>', func = switch_picker },\r\n    },\r\n  })\r\n\r\n```",
